// IRIW.
//
// Independent reads of independent writes: two readers disagree about the order
//   of two writes to different locations.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: SC forbids, TSO
//     forbids, Coherence allows, RC11 allows, RC17 allows, OD-LSO allows.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     x86-TSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     RC11z allows. Equivalent to RC11 (zoo edge).
//     MRD allows. RC11 allows it, and MRD is weaker than RC11 (zoo edge RC11 ->
//       MRD).
//     CC allows. Causal allows it, and CC is weaker.
//     PRAM allows. PC allows it, and PRAM is weaker.
//     Slow allows. PRAM allows it, and Slow is weaker.
//     Local allows. Slow allows it, and Local is weaker.
//     RYW allows. PRAM allows it, and RYW is weaker.
//     MR allows. PRAM allows it, and MR is weaker.
//     MW allows. PRAM allows it, and MW is weaker.
//     WFR allows. Causal allows it, and WFR is weaker.
//   the models' definitions:
//     PC allows. Each location has one write, so the shared order per location
//       says nothing about the order across x and y.
//     Causal allows. The two writes are causally unrelated, so the readers'
//       views may order them differently.
//     POCausal allows. Per object, each reader sees one write or none; nothing
//       relates x to y.
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: none. RA, SRA and WRA
//     are defined on release stores and acquire loads, and this program has
//     other accesses.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  x := 1
} ||| {
  y := 1
} ||| {
  r0 := x;
  r1 := y
} ||| {
  r2 := y;
  r3 := x
}
%%
allow (r0 = 1 && r1 = 0 && r2 = 1 && r3 = 0) [Coherence, RC11, RC11z, RC17,
                                              OD-LSO, MRD, CC, PC, PRAM,
                                              Causal, Slow, Local, POCausal,
                                              RYW, MR, MW, WFR]
forbid (r0 = 1 && r1 = 0 && r2 = 1 && r3 = 0) [SC, VbD, TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO]
